WEBVTT

00:00:58.763 --> 00:01:02.391
becoming more prosperous,
more fair, more free.

00:01:03.351 --> 00:01:07.021
In 2004 and 2013,

00:01:07.063 --> 00:01:11.317
we marched for democracy,
and we defeated autocracy.

00:01:12.026 --> 00:01:15.947
So I was stunned
when the windows crushed in.

00:01:17.156 --> 00:01:18.282
I froze.

00:01:18.908 --> 00:01:22.036
Speechless, motionless,

00:01:22.078 --> 00:01:24.288
absolutely helpless.

00:01:25.123 --> 00:01:27.500
That was my first lesson of war.

00:01:28.543 --> 00:01:32.421
What you cherish can be taken
from you in a moment.